descriptions.job-0sdid6c:
&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Financial Systems organization partners with Stripe’s People organization to build trusted, intuitive products for employees, managers, and People professionals. We aim to make routine interactions simple and self-service while ensuring that work requiring judgment or care reaches the right person with the right context.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our products connect data, knowledge, workflows, and systems that span the employee experience. We are building toward a future in which employees and managers can get accurate answers and complete common tasks without navigating fragmented tools, while People teams can spend more time on the work that benefits most from&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own products that make it easier for employees to get accurate guidance and complete common People-related tasks, while helping People team focus their expertise on work that requires judgment and care. You will identify the highest-impact user problems, define the product strategy and roadmap, and lead products from discovery through delivery, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to shape a growing product area at the intersection of employee experience, enterprise systems, data, and applied AI. You will help develop agentic products that connect people to accurate guidance, automate appropriate actions, and help People practitioners focus their expertise where it matters most. Success requires understanding the capabilities and limitations of AI and machine learning when applied to business-critical, regulated, and strictly governed problems. You will also use AI-enabled tools throughout the product development lifecycle to accelerate discovery, prototyping, requirements development, evaluation, and iteration while protecting employee trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of employees, managers, and People practitioners, then translate their most important needs into a focused product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own products end to end, from problem discovery and strategy through delivery, adoption, measurement, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design coherent experiences that connect fragmented data, knowledge, workflows, and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the People org, engineering, data, security, legal, and others to make sound product and architecture tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define measures to understand adoption, engagement, and impact for products and develop insights into the metrics to guide improvements to the product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop agentic People products and define where systems may recommend, act, escalate, or defer to accountable human judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-enabled tools throughout product development and help establish effective practices for AI-assisted discovery, prototyping, specification, testing, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead adoption and establish sustainable ownership and support for products that change established ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management or equivalent experience leading the development of software products for internal or external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently navigating ambiguity, identifying the underlying user problem, and converting broad strategies into focused product roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping products that connect workflows, data, and multiple systems or teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of AI and machine-learning product development beyond using LLM-based tools, including model capabilities, data requirements, evaluation methods, failure modes, privacy considerations, and the tradeoffs between probabilistic, deterministic, and human-led approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-enabled tools to improve the quality and speed of product discovery, prototyping, delivery, or evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead across functions and build alignment among stakeholders with different expertise, incentives, and responsibilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing products where user trust, privacy, permissions, or other sensitive requirements are central to the product experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with employee products, human-resources technology, People operations, enterprise workflow, or manager-facing tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building governed data products, self-service experiences, or role-aware applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping agentic or AI/ML-powered products for People or another trust-sensitive domain, with appropriate evaluation, privacy safeguards, escalation, and human accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading adoption and organizational change for products that replace established manual processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-0e6i1f8:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title: &lt;/strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Regulatory Operations Manager (Mexico)&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Mexico – Hybrid&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Type:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-time&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting to:&lt;/strong&gt; Country Manager, Mexico (solid line) / Global Chief Compliance Officer (dotted line)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Telcoin is a global fintech company focused on developing innovative financial products and infrastructure at the intersection of telecommunications, payments, and digital assets (Stablecoins).&lt;br&gt;Established in 2017, Telcoin operates through entities across multiple international markets and continues to expand its regulated financial services footprint.&lt;br&gt;As we develop our business in Mexico, we are seeking an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Regulatory Operations Manager&lt;/strong&gt; who can lead our local compliance function while also taking a hands-on role in regulatory applications, licensing initiatives, and broader business operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Compliance &amp;amp; Regulatory Operations Manager will be a key member of Telcoin Mexico&#39;s leadership team.&lt;br&gt;The role will have a &lt;strong&gt;solid-line reporting relationship to the Country Manager in Mexico&lt;/strong&gt;, while maintaining a &lt;strong&gt;dotted-line relationship to Telcoin&#39;s Global Chief Compliance Officer&lt;/strong&gt; and working closely with Telcoin&#39;s global Compliance, Legal, Product, Operations, Finance, and Risk teams.&amp;nbsp; This is a hands-on leadership role, not a purely advisory one. You will move between regulatory interpretation and practical execution: leading Telcoin&#39;s financial institution application from preparation through regulatory review, owning the local AML/CFT program end to end, and acting as a trusted advisor to the Country Manager on how regulatory requirements shape the business, including virtual-assest-related obligations.&amp;nbsp; The person joining us should therefore be comfortable working in an environment where regulatory, operational, and commercial workstreams frequently overlap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Strategy &amp;amp; Licensing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Country Manager, Global Chief Compliance Officer, Legal team, senior management, and external regulatory advisers to execute Telcoin&#39;s regulatory strategy in Mexico.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a hands-on role in preparing regulatory applications, supporting documentation, policies, procedures, business plans, operating models, risk assessments, and responses to regulatory inquiries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Telcoin&#39;s planned application for authorization as an &lt;strong&gt;financial institution&lt;/strong&gt; and help manage the application and authorization process from preparation through regulatory review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support other registrations and regulatory initiatives relevant to Telcoin&#39;s business model, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SAT registration and ongoing obligations relating to &lt;strong&gt;Actividades Vulnerables involving virtual assets&lt;/strong&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;applicable CNBV registrations or authorizations;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;additional financial-services permissions that may become necessary as the Mexican business develops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate regulatory projects across Telcoin&#39;s local and global teams and external advisers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track regulatory submissions, outstanding requirements, dependencies, deadlines, and regulator requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key point of contact with Mexican regulators and governmental authorities where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AML / CFT &amp;amp; Compliance Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, maintain, and continuously improve Telcoin Mexico&#39;s AML/CFT and financial-crime compliance framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain local policies and procedures in accordance with Mexican law while ensuring appropriate alignment with Telcoin Group&#39;s global compliance standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct and maintain AML/CFT and other regulatory risk assessments applicable to the Mexican business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee customer due diligence, KYC, enhanced due diligence, beneficial ownership identification, sanctions screening, transaction monitoring, and related financial-crime controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure required regulatory notices, reports, and other filings are submitted accurately and within applicable deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review potentially suspicious customer or transactional activity and coordinate escalation and reporting processes where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain appropriate compliance records, registers, evidence, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor regulatory developments in Mexico and assess their impact on Telcoin&#39;s products and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Global Compliance team to continuously strengthen Telcoin&#39;s compliance framework and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support regulatory inspections, audits, information requests, and remediation programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business &amp;amp; Regulatory Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will also act as a &lt;strong&gt;hands-on business partner to the Country Manager&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities may include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the Country Manager with regulatory, operational, and administrative requirements involved in establishing and scaling Telcoin&#39;s Mexican business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping translate regulatory requirements into practical product and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with Product and Engineering teams to ensure regulatory requirements are appropriately incorporated into product development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinating with banks, payment partners, vendors, consultants, lawyers, auditors, and other third parties required to establish Telcoin&#39;s operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting with business applications, due diligence requests, questionnaires, banking relationships, vendor onboarding, and regulatory documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the development of operating procedures and internal controls as the local organization grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking ownership of projects outside of traditional compliance responsibilities where necessary to help establish and grow the Mexican business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who is comfortable &lt;strong&gt;rolling up their sleeves and getting things done&lt;/strong&gt;, rather than operating solely as a policy or advisory function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Law, Finance, Business Administration, Accounting, Economics, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant professional experience in compliance, regulatory affairs, financial crime, legal/regulatory operations, or a closely related role within Mexico.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong practical knowledge of the Mexican financial-services regulatory environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with or interacting with Mexican regulators such as &lt;strong&gt;CNBV, SAT, SHCP/UIF, or Banco de México&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with AML/CFT, KYC/CDD, transaction monitoring, regulatory reporting, and compliance controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing regulatory documentation and coordinating complex regulatory or licensing projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently manage projects involving multiple internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and analytical skills with excellent attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial mindset and ability to understand how regulatory requirements affect products and business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a fast-moving environment where processes and regulatory structures are still being built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in &lt;strong&gt;Spanish and English&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resident in Mexico.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience working for an Financial Institution&lt;strong&gt; fintech, payments company, digital asset company, bank, money transmitter, or other regulated financial institution in Mexico&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience supporting an Financial Institution authorization or another CNBV financial institution licensing process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing a compliance program or regulated operation from an early stage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Mexican regulation relating to virtual assets and Actividades Vulnerables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with cryptocurrency, blockchain, stablecoins, digital wallets, cross-border payments, or other digital financial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CNBV certification in PLD/FT/FPADM&lt;/strong&gt;, or eligibility and willingness to obtain the applicable certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within an international organization and coordinating with global Compliance, Legal, Product, and Operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Person We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines the mindset of a &lt;strong&gt;compliance professional, regulatory project manager, and business operator&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br&gt;You should be comfortable interpreting regulation and discussing technical compliance requirements with lawyers and regulators, but equally comfortable opening a spreadsheet, preparing an application, coordinating documentation, working with a banking partner, reviewing a product workflow, or helping the Country Manager solve an operational problem.&lt;br&gt;Telcoin Mexico is entering an important stage of its development, including preparations for additional financial-services authorization. This role provides an opportunity to help build the regulatory and operational foundation of the business rather than simply maintain an established compliance program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Interested candidates should submit a resume outlining their relevant experience, particularly any experience involving Mexican financial-services regulation, AML/CFT, fintech, payments, digital assets, or regulatory licensing.&lt;br&gt;Please highlight any relevant professional certifications, including CNBV AML/CFT certification, and any direct experience with a financial institution authorization processes in Mexico.&lt;br&gt;Telcoin is an equal opportunity employer committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace. We encourage qualified candidates from all backgrounds to apply.&lt;/p&gt;

descriptions.job-1cbbbn8:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Join us in building the future of finance.&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to democratize finance for all. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cerulli.com/press-releases/cerulli-anticipates-124-trillion-in-wealth-will-transfer-through-2048&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;An estimated $124 trillion of assets&lt;/a&gt; will be inherited by younger generations in the next two decades. The largest transfer of wealth in human history. If you’re ready to be at the epicenter of this historic cultural and financial shift, keep reading.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the team + role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team, applying frontier technologies to the world&#39;s biggest financial problems. We&#39;re looking for bold thinkers. Sharp problem-solvers. Builders who are wired to make an impact. Robinhood isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it&#39;s where ambitious people do the best work of their careers. We&#39;re a high-performing, fast-moving team with ethics at the center of everything we do. Expectations are high, and so are the rewards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The PeopleX (People Experience) team&#39;s mission is to build a high-performance culture and enhance employee experience by driving impactful programs, hiring top talent, and enabling community across Robinhood.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a People Partner Intern, you&#39;ll work on meaningful projects that support our People team&#39;s strategy—bringing insights, operations, and collaboration together to create a thriving workplace!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in our New York office, with in-person attendance expected at least 3 days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Robinhood, we believe in the power of in-person work to accelerate progress, spark innovation, and strengthen community. Our office experience is intentional, energizing, and designed to fully support high-performing teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support key PeopleX initiatives, including business support and program delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze employee feedback, operational data, and program outcomes to surface trends and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with COEs across PX and the business to solve challenging people-related problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a strong, inclusive employee experience by helping deliver meaningful internal programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently enrolled in a full-time undergraduate or graduate program, ideally in Business, Human Resources, Organizational Behavior, or a related field; prior HR experience (internship, co-op, or similar) preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and energized by a fast-paced environment centered on learning and contributing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and detail-oriented, with a knack for project coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills; comfortable collaborating across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Workday and Google Suite is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market competitive compensation structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly lifestyle wallet for personal wellness, learning and development, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to the best AI tools on the market and continuous AI skill-building for every employee, technical or not&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time away including company holidays, paid time off, and sick time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lively office environment with catered meals, fully stocked kitchens, and geo-specific commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot; data-sheets-value=&quot;{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;The expected salary range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. This role is also eligible to participate in a Robinhood bonus plan.\n\nUS Zone 1: $24.65 - $29 per hour\nUS Zone 2: $24.65 - $29 per hour\nUS Zone 3: $23.8 - $28 per hour&amp;quot;}&quot; data-sheets-userformat=&quot;{&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:4540,&amp;quot;5&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;5&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0}},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:3},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;4&amp;quot;:1}]},&amp;quot;6&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;5&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0}},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:3},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;4&amp;quot;:1}]},&amp;quot;7&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;5&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0}},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:3},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;4&amp;quot;:1}]},&amp;quot;8&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;5&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0}},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:3},{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;4&amp;quot;:1}]},&amp;quot;10&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;11&amp;quot;:4,&amp;quot;15&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;}&quot; data-sheets-formula=&quot;=if(R[0]C6=&amp;quot;Salary&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;The expected salary range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. This role is also eligible to participate in a Robinhood bonus plan and Robinhood’s equity plan.&amp;quot;&amp;amp;char(10)&amp;amp; char(10)&amp;amp; R[0]C15 &amp;amp; char(10)&amp;amp; R[0]C14 &amp;amp; char(10)&amp;amp; R[0]C13, &amp;quot;The expected salary range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. This role is also eligible to participate in a Robinhood bonus plan.&amp;quot;&amp;amp;char(10)&amp;amp; char(10)&amp;amp; R[0]C15 &amp;amp; char(10)&amp;amp; R[0]C14 &amp;amp; char(10)&amp;amp; R[0]C13)&quot;&gt;Base pay for the successful applicant will depend on a variety of job-related factors, which may include education, training, experience, location, business needs, or market demands. The expected hourly range for this role is based on the location where the work will be performed and is aligned to one of 3 compensation zones. For other locations not listed, compensation can be discussed with your recruiter during the interview process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 (Menlo Park, CA; New York, NY; Bellevue, WA; Washington, DC)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$38&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$38 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/benefits&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about our Total Rewards, which vary by region and entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If our mission energizes you and you’re ready to build the future of finance, we look forward to seeing your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Robinhood provides equal opportunity for all applicants, offers reasonable accommodations upon request, and complies with applicable equal employment and privacy laws. Inclusion is built into how we hire and work—welcoming different backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences so everyone can do their best. Please review the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.robinhood.com/applicantprivacypolicy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt; for your country of application.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

descriptions.job-1bimxx0:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About ComplyAdvantage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ComplyAdvantage is the financial industry’s leading source of AI-driven financial crime risk data and detection technology. Our mission is to neutralize the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing, corruption, and other financial crimes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than 1,000 companies globally rely on us to navigate risk through the world’s only real-time database of people and companies. Backed by Goldman Sachs, Ontario Teachers’, Index Ventures, and Balderton Capital, we have raised over $100M to date. After growing our team by 40% last year, we are scaling from 500 to 600+ people - and our SDR team is the engine behind that growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a people-leadership role first. As Head of Business Development for EMEA, you own the outbound business development (BDR) function across the region — hiring, developing, and leading a team of BDRs whose job is to generate qualified pipeline for our new-business sales organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will set the outbound strategy, build the ramp and coaching systems that make reps successful, and create the career pathways that turn strong BDRs into future account executives. Your success is measured by the performance, retention, and progression of the team you build — and by the quality of pipeline they generate for the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and coach the team. Run daily coaching, call reviews, and 1:1s that raise the performance of every BDR — developing outbound craft, resilience, and commercial judgment across the group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the hiring bar. Run a structured, competency-based interview process, and keep a bench of talent ahead of demand so the team can scale without dropping quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design onboarding and ramp. Build and run a structured 90-day onboarding program with clear milestone gates, so new hires reach full productivity faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build career pathways. Maintain a competency framework with assessable junior and senior behaviors, and create clear BDR-to-AE progression that helps you attract and retain ambitious reps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the outbound strategy. Define account prioritization, ideal-customer-profile targeting, messaging, and multi-channel sequencing across EMEA, in partnership with Sales and Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own pipeline generation. Carry the team’s qualified-pipeline target, forecast opportunities into the new-business funnel, and use data to diagnose and fix what is not working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across the business. Work with Revenue Operations on tooling, routing, reporting, and compensation design, and align closely with Marketing on account-based programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on performance. Give sales leadership a clear, evidence-based view of team health, ramp, and pipeline contribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proficient with:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cognism&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales Nav&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clay&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building multi-outreach&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insights into performing channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;People-management experience is essential. We are looking for someone with a strong track record of managing an outbound BDR or SDR team — you have hired, coached, and retained reps and led a team to target, not only carried a number yourself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team leadership. Proven experience leading and developing outbound BDRs/SDRs, with a genuine interest in growing people and a record of moving reps into more senior roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building the function. Experience designing or scaling onboarding, ramp, coaching, and performance frameworks — not just running the ones you inherited.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outbound craft. Strong command of prospecting, multi-channel sequencing, and qualification (MEDDIC or a similar framework), with the ability to teach it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data fluency. Comfortable in Salesforce and reporting tools, using metrics to manage a team, forecast pipeline, and make decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial background. Experience selling or generating pipeline in B2B SaaS; exposure to RegTech, FinTech, financial services, or compliance is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The right blend. The emotional intelligence to develop people, and the operational rigor to run a team at scale across multiple markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice to have&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or managing teams across multiple EMEA markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with anti-money laundering (AML), sanctions, or wider financial crime compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Marketing on account-based experience (ABX) or account-based marketing (ABM) programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How we work&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our values shape how this team operates, and we hire for them:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make a safer world. The work matters — we help stop the movement of funds that fuel serious crime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar. We hold a high standard for ourselves and each other, and we keep getting better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See it, own it, drive it forward. We take ownership and follow through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Win as one team. We succeed together, across functions and regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to empower every business to eliminate financial crime.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By harnessing AI, a unified platform, and an extensive partner ecosystem, we help customers turn compliance into a catalyst for growth, operational resilience, and enduring regulatory trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than 3,000 enterprises across 75 countries rely on our end-to-end platform and the world’s most comprehensive financial crime risk intelligence. With full-stack agentic automation, we help organizations automate up to 95% of KYC, AML, and sanctions reviews, cut onboarding times by 50%, reduce false positives by 70%, and handle 7x more work with the same staff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ComplyAdvantage is headquartered in London and has global hubs in New York, Lisbon, Singapore, and Cluj-Napoca. It is backed by Balderton Capital, Index Ventures, Ontario Teachers’ Pension Plan, Goldman Sachs, and Andreessen Horowitz. Learn more about compliance re-engineered for the age of AI at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://complyadvantage.com&quot;&gt;complyadvantage.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

descriptions.job-196wlx0:
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Startup SaaS Platform team works with European startups in one of Stripe’s must-win segments. At Stripe, SaaS platforms are companies that use Stripe to embed payments and make financial services a core part of their product. Their partnership with Stripe is vital to their business success. Examples include Shopify, Mindbody, and Lightspeed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SaaS platforms are a global priority for Stripe. Our team identifies and develops Stripe’s future strategic accounts in Europe. We identify and partner with high-potential companies, helping them leverage Stripe’s solutions to better support their users, scale globally, and create new revenue streams through monetisation of payments and financial services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Grower Account Executive on the Startup SaaS Platforms team, you’ll drive Stripe’s future growth through account expansion and client retention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll advise businesses on how to optimise their operations using Stripe solutions. You’ll help users understand how Stripe’s modern financial infrastructure supports their growth ambitions and provides a competitive edge for their business or product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage and cultivate a named list of existing user accounts, while crafting account plans to expand business and retain clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand users’ pain points and Stripe’s value for SaaS platform clients, proposing tailored solutions that support their long-term growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide clients through complex evaluations of Stripe solutions for SaaS platforms, working with cross-functional teams across Product, Risk, and Operations to move new projects through activation and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic programs that deepen product adoption and maximise effective utilisation across the current user base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster executive relationships with stakeholders at existing clients to drive retention and identify expansion opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional teams on shared initiatives that drive internal efficiency and broader business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Stripe’s go-to-market priority to expand the user base and optimise the renewals motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a curious, well-rounded strategic seller who builds strong relationships with Stripe’s clients in this key segment. You’re comfortable owning your territory and balancing a mix of high-value, strategic deals with smaller, high-velocity deal cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re solution-oriented and adaptable, with an interest in developing yourself and getting things done. You enjoy highly technical sales cycles and working with a diverse group of internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–6+ years of experience in a client-facing or closing sales role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical ecosystems and manage complex sales cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing projects with input from cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build relationships with technical customers, work with a wide range of internal and external stakeholders, contribute to team success, and share knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivation to operate in a highly ambiguous and fluid environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a sales or customer-facing role at a high-growth technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort interpreting and discussing API-first solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-0p65r90:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a 12-week internship during summer 2027.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the People Analytics team within our People Success Function. This team provides intelligence and tools that empower leaders to make key people decisions and drive business value. You&#39;ll support analyses across the employee lifecycle, help streamline reporting processes, and contribute to solutions that measure the impact of complex People programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze People data across the employee lifecycle to identify trends and surface actionable insights for leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI tools to accelerate data exploration and enable self-service access to insights for stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype AI-driven workflow automations for recurring reports, anomaly detection, and data-quality checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad hoc data requests by building and maintaining spreadsheets and dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with stakeholders to improve dashboard navigation, access, and self-service reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with team members to develop executive presentations that translate data into clear narratives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a degree or certificate in an analytical discipline (e.g., data science, statistics, I/O psychology, business analytics, or related field).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience analyzing and manipulating data using spreadsheets (Excel, Google Sheets) with the ability to translate findings into actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to communicate data insights clearly in both written and verbal formats to non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of handling highly sensitive or confidential data with discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with at least one data visualization tool (Looker, Tableau, PowerBI, or OneModel) or basic SQL knowledge is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Position ID: P78055&lt;/p&gt;
